course: dictionary
lesson: 5979
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around a word, tells you which meaning is meant. Mayflower is one of these words. «The Pilgrims came on the Mayflower in 1620» tells you it is a ship, because people travel on a ship, not on a flower.
explain: The same word can also be a plant. A mayflower is a plant that flowers in spring, such as hawthorn in Britain. So a sentence about hedges covered in mayflower is about blossom, not a boat. Ask yourself: is this sentence about a voyage, or about spring?
explain: A capital letter is another clue. The Mayflower, with a big M, is the famous ship, and the Mayflower Pilgrims are the people who sailed on it. Put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: The Mayflower was the ship that carried English settlers, now called the Pilgrims, across the Atlantic from Plymouth in England to America.
fact: The Mayflower started Plymouth Colony, where the settlers made their new home.
fact: A «mayflower» is any of several plants that flower in spring, especially hawthorn in Britain and the trailing arbutus in North America.
fact: The mayflower is the floral symbol of Nova Scotia in Canada and of Massachusetts in the USA.
fact: Phrases like «the Mayflower Pilgrims» and «the Mayflower Compact» use the ship's name to point to one specific story.
exercise: «The Pilgrims came on the Mayflower in 1620.» What is the Mayflower in this sentence? | A type of flower | A school | *A ship | A market in a town
exercise: Mum says the hawthorn hedge is covered in mayflower. What does mayflower mean? | A sunny day in May | *A plant that flowers in spring | A ship that sailed across the Atlantic | A plant that flowers in winter
exercise: Which sentence uses mayflower to mean the ship? | «The mayflower bloomed early this spring.» | *«The Mayflower set sail from Plymouth in England.» | «The mayflower smelled sweet in the garden.» | «We picked mayflowers in the park.»
test: «The Mayflower carried settlers across the Atlantic.» Which clue shows it means a ship, not a flower? | It starts with M | It has the word flower in it | *Carried settlers across the Atlantic | It is a long word
test: Which place has the mayflower as its floral symbol? | Australia | *Massachusetts in the USA | Scotland | Kenya
exam: «The Mayflower sailed from Plymouth with settlers on board.» Which clue tells you Mayflower means the ship? | It grows in spring | *Sailed from Plymouth with settlers on board | It is a very old word | It is a plant with white petals
